# reject-obo-undeclared — on-behalf-of must name a declared actor or human;
# a binding naming an undeclared node is ill-formed at apply (§6). The delegate
# holds no grant, so no other rule (in particular no-amplification over an
# empty delegator set) can be the cause: only the declared-delegator rule rejects.
actor a on-behalf-of ghost
actor b
gate g risk low grant b[deploy:low]
cord g -> master
